---
title: SPI - shared four-wire bus
---
%% NO DOCUMENTED PINS in the driver - the application opens the bus.
%% SPI5 on PF7/PF8/PF9 is already wired on this board and is shared by the
%% on-board LCD and gyro, so any extra device needs a CS pin of its own.
%% Free pins for chip selects: PC11, PC12, PC13, PE2, PE3.
%% Only ONE CS may be low at a time or two devices drive MISO together.
%% Idle every CS HIGH; a floating CS makes a device respond to another's traffic.
%% Devices on the same bus must tolerate the same mode and clock rate, or the
%% bus has to be reconfigured between transfers.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1 - SPI5 master"]
        SCK["PF7 - SCK"]
        MISO["PF8 - MISO"]
        MOSI["PF9 - MOSI"]
        CS1["PC1 - CS gyro, on board"]
        CS2["PC2 - CS LCD, on board"]
        CS3["PC13 - CS spare device"]
    end

    D1["L3GD20 gyro - on board"]
    D2["ILI9341 LCD - on board"]
    D3["Your device - flash, MCP2515, XPT2046..."]

    SCK --> D1
    SCK --> D2
    SCK --> D3
    MOSI --> D1
    MOSI --> D2
    MOSI --> D3
    MISO --- D1
    MISO --- D2
    MISO --- D3
    CS1 --> D1
    CS2 --> D2
    CS3 --> D3
